{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"dfa39beb","metadata":{"id":"dfa39beb"},"source":["# CSA47 – Deep Learning · Assignment 1\n","## Analyse the Mathematical and ML Foundations of a Crop-Disease Screening System (\"AgriVision\")\n","\n","**Name:** Padmanabhan &nbsp;|&nbsp; **Reg. No.:** 192324076 &nbsp;|&nbsp; B.Tech AI & DS, SIMATS Engineering\n","\n","**Dataset:** PlantVillage – *Tomato* subset (10 classes: 9 diseases + healthy, ≈18,160 images), resized to **64 × 64 grayscale → 4,096 features**.\n","Task 12 additionally uses all **38 PlantVillage classes**.\n","\n","**Conventions used throughout**\n","* Every formula is stated before it is used; each numeric result is printed to **4 decimal places**.\n","* Information-theoretic quantities use **log base 2 (bits)**.\n","* Hyper-parameters are chosen on the **validation** set; the **test** set is touched only in Task 9.\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"9de676bf","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-12T04:09:32.907141Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-12T04:09:32.906861Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-12T04:09:36.445115Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-12T04:09:36.442100Z"},"id":"9de676bf"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os, re, time, pickle, subprocess, warnings\n","import numpy as np, pandas as pd, matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, cross_val_score, StratifiedKFold\n","from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n","from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n","from sklearn.pipeline import make_pipeline\n","from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n","from sklearn.neighbors import KNeighborsClassifier\n","from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n","from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier\n","from sklearn.metrics.pairwise import euclidean_distances\n","from sklearn.metrics import (accuracy_score, precision_recall_fscore_support,\n","                             confusion_matrix, ConfusionMatrixDisplay)\n","warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n","np.set_printoptions(precision=4, suppress=True)\n","pd.set_option('display.float_format', lambda v: f'{v:.4f}')\n","plt.rcParams.update({'figure.dpi': 110, 'axes.grid': True, 'grid.alpha': .3})\n","\n","SEED = 42\n","rng = np.random.default_rng(SEED)\n","IMG = 64\n","DATA_DIR = None          # optional: your own PlantVillage folder (one sub-folder per class); None = download from GitHub\n","BASE = '/content' if os.path.isdir('/content') else '.'\n","CACHE = f'{BASE}/agrivision_cache.npz'\n","PV_ROOT = f'{BASE}/PlantVillage-Dataset'\n","TEST_MODE = os.environ.get('AGRI_TEST') == '1'   # synthetic smoke-test only; leave unset in Colab\n","PER_CLASS_38 = 150       # images per class for the 38-class experiment (Task 12)\n","def f4(x): return float(np.round(x, 4))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"6f8c83b6","metadata":{"id":"6f8c83b6"},"source":["### Data Collection & Preprocessing\n","Downloads PlantVillage from GitHub (sparse checkout: only the files needed) or reads a local folder, converts every image to **grayscale**, resizes to **64 × 64** and scales pixels to $[0,1]$:\n","$$x_{ij}=\\frac{\\text{pixel}_{ij}}{255}\\in[0,1],\\qquad \\mathbf{x}=\\text{vec}(X)\\in\\mathbb{R}^{4096}$$\n","Keeps the 10 tomato classes (Tasks 1–11) and a per-class sample of all 38 classes (Task 12). Arrays are cached so re-runs are instant."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"604c4a8b","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-12T04:09:36.450523Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-12T04:09:36.449714Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-12T04:12:24.132056Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-12T04:12:24.129143Z"},"id":"604c4a8b","outputId":"b6981db4-2186-48df-dbfe-3839c28b38a3","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791960913482,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":115818,"user":{"displayName":"Padmanabhan S","userId":"00156433950367292426"}}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Downloading PlantVillage images from GitHub (one-time, a few minutes)...\n","Tomato subset: (18160, 64, 64) -> (18160, 4096) | classes: 10\n","Bacterial_spot                          2127\n","Early_blight                            1000\n","Late_blight                             1909\n","Leaf_Mold                                952\n","Septoria_leaf_spot                      1771\n","Spider_mites Two-spotted_spider_mite    1676\n","Target_Spot                             1404\n","Tomato_Yellow_Leaf_Curl_Virus           5357\n","Tomato_mosaic_virus                      373\n","healthy                                 1591\n","Name: images, dtype: int64\n","38-class sample: (5700, 4096) classes: 38\n"]}],"source":["def fetch_plantvillage(root, per_other):\n","    # sparse, blob-less clone: downloads only the chosen image files (all tomato + per_other per other class)\n","    print('Downloading PlantVillage images from GitHub (one-time, a few minutes)...')\n","    url = 'https://github.com/spMohanty/PlantVillage-Dataset.git'\n","    if not os.path.isdir(root):\n","        subprocess.run(['git', 'clone', '-q', '--depth', '1', '--filter=blob:none', '--no-checkout', url, root], check=True)\n","    files = subprocess.run(['git', '-C', root, 'ls-tree', '-r', '--name-only', 'HEAD', 'raw/grayscale'],\n","                           capture_output=True, text=True, check=True).stdout.splitlines()\n","    by_cls = {}\n","    for f in files: by_cls.setdefault(f.split('/')[2], []).append(f)\n","    pick = [f for c, fs in sorted(by_cls.items())\n","            for f in (fs if c.lower().startswith('tomato') else sorted(fs)[:per_other])]\n","    pats = '\\n'.join('/' + re.sub(r'([\\[\\]*?\\\\!#])', r'\\\\\\1', f) for f in pick)\n","    subprocess.run(['git', '-C', root, 'sparse-checkout', 'set', '--no-cone', '--stdin'], input=pats, text=True, check=True)\n","    subprocess.run(['git', '-C', root, 'checkout', '-q', 'HEAD'], check=True)\n","    return os.path.join(root, 'raw', 'grayscale')\n","\n","def load_folder(root):\n","    from PIL import Image\n","    names = sorted(d for d in os.listdir(root) if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(root, d)))\n","    Xs, ys = [], []\n","    for i, n in enumerate(names):\n","        for f in sorted(os.listdir(os.path.join(root, n))):\n","            try:\n","                im = Image.open(os.path.join(root, n, f)).convert('L').resize((IMG, IMG))\n","                Xs.append(np.asarray(im, np.float32) / 255.0); ys.append(i)\n","            except Exception:\n","                pass\n","    return np.stack(Xs), np.array(ys), names\n","\n","def make_synthetic(K, per):\n","    # smoke-test stand-in only (class = position of a dark blob on a bright leaf)\n","    yy, xx = np.mgrid[0:IMG, 0:IMG]\n","    Xs, ys = [], []\n","    for c in range(K):\n","        cy, cx = 12 + (c * 7) % 40, 12 + (c * 13) % 40\n","        for _ in range(per):\n","            img = 0.6 + 0.1 * rng.standard_normal() - 0.4 * np.exp(-((yy - cy - rng.normal(0, 3))**2 + (xx - cx - rng.normal(0, 3))**2) / 60)\n","            Xs.append(np.clip(img + 0.05 * rng.standard_normal((IMG, IMG)), 0, 1).astype(np.float32)); ys.append(c)\n","    return np.stack(Xs), np.array(ys), [f'Tomato___synthetic_{c}' for c in range(K)]\n","\n","if TEST_MODE:\n","    Xall, yall, names_all = make_synthetic(12, 260)\n","elif os.path.exists(CACHE):\n","    d = np.load(CACHE, allow_pickle=True); Xall, yall, names_all = d['X'], d['y'], list(d['names'])\n","else:\n","    Xall, yall, names_all = load_folder(DATA_DIR or fetch_plantvillage(PV_ROOT, PER_CLASS_38))\n","    # keep tomato images + a per-class sample of all 38 classes (keeps the cache small)\n","    keep = np.zeros(len(yall), bool)\n","    for c, n in enumerate(names_all):\n","        idx = np.where(yall == c)[0]\n","        keep[idx if n.lower().startswith('tomato') else rng.permutation(idx)[:PER_CLASS_38]] = True\n","    Xall, yall = Xall[keep], yall[keep]\n","    np.savez_compressed(CACHE, X=Xall, y=yall, names=np.array(names_all))\n","\n","# ---- 38-class sample (Task 12)\n","idx38 = np.concatenate([rng.permutation(np.where(yall == c)[0])[:PER_CLASS_38] for c in np.unique(yall)])\n","X38, y38 = Xall[idx38].reshape(len(idx38), -1), yall[idx38]\n","\n","# ---- Tomato subset (Tasks 1-11)\n","tom = [c for c, n in enumerate(names_all) if n.lower().startswith('tomato')]\n","if TEST_MODE: tom = tom[:10]\n","mask = np.isin(yall, tom)\n","X_img = Xall[mask]                                   # (N, 64, 64)\n","remap = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(tom)}\n","y = np.array([remap[c] for c in yall[mask]])         # (N,)\n","CLASSES = [names_all[c].split('___')[-1] for c in tom]\n","K = len(CLASSES)\n","X = X_img.reshape(len(X_img), -1)                    # (N, 4096)\n","print('Tomato subset:', X_img.shape, '->', X.shape, '| classes:', K)\n","print(pd.Series(np.bincount(y), index=CLASSES, name='images'))\n","print('38-class sample:', X38.shape, 'classes:', len(np.unique(y38)))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b4e25af3","metadata":{"id":"b4e25af3"},"source":["### Train / Validation / Test Split\n","**Stratified split** keeps every class's proportion equal in all three subsets:\n","$$P_{train}(y=k)\\approx P_{val}(y=k)\\approx P_{test}(y=k)\\quad\\forall k$$\n","70 % train (fit), 15 % validation (choose hyper-parameters), 15 % test (locked until Task 9)."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"9bde924c","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-12T04:12:24.138243Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-12T04:12:24.137785Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-12T04:12:24.480074Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-12T04:12:24.477764Z"},"id":"9bde924c","outputId":"2f2e08ba-0c4e-40d3-90b1-c2bd56e48372","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":380},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791960913716,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":229,"user":{"displayName":"Padmanabhan S","userId":"00156433950367292426"}}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["tr