     columns=['L1', 'L2', 'Linf'])\n","display(nt)\n","print('Check (numpy.linalg.norm):', [f4(np.linalg.norm(x_one, o)) for o in (1, 2, np.inf)])"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a9af8dfd","metadata":{"id":"a9af8dfd"},"source":["**Which norm for which purpose**\n","* **L¹** – sums every pixel's deviation: robust to a few outliers, total \"ink\"; basis of L1 regularisation (sparsity).\n","* **L²** – Euclidean length: used by k-NN distance, PCA reconstruction error and L2 weight decay; dominated by large deviations.\n","* **L∞** – the single worst pixel: detects a saturated/clipped pixel or the max adversarial perturbation; ignores everything else.\n","\n","Since $\\|x\\|_\\infty \\le \\|x\\|_2 \\le \\|x\\|_1 \\le \\sqrt{n}\\|x\\|_2$, with $n=4096$ the L¹ value is much larger than L² – the spread between them shows how *spread out* (not sparse) the image energy is."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"0b2349a6","metadata":{"id":"0b2349a6"},"source":[">compare the L1/L2 ratio with √4096 = 64 — is the information spread over many pixels or concentrated?"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"e5baee6b","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-12T04:12:25.865504Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-12T04:12:25.865160Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-12T04:12:26.789669Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-12T04:12:26.787435Z"},"id":"e5baee6b","outputId":"a99a7e80-d4ae-457f-cbc2-06ecd4bead54","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791960915520,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":121,"user":{"displayName":"Padmanabhan S","userId":"00156433950367292426"}}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Resize + grayscale : 196608 -> 4096 values  (kept 2.0833 % ; colour cue lost)\n","Normalise /255     : range [0,255] -> [0.0, 1.0] ; mean 0.4514999985694885, std 0.15520000457763672\n","Standardise (train stats only): per-pixel mean -> 0.0, std -> 1.0\n","Flattening: distances identical after randomly shuffling pixel order -> True\n","Split: max class-proportion difference train vs test = 0.0002\n"]}],"source":["# Effect of each preprocessing step on the information available\n","orig_vals, kept = 256 * 256 * 3, IMG * IMG\n","print(f'Resize + grayscale : {orig_vals} -> {kept} values  (kept {f4(kept / orig_vals * 100)} % ; colour cue lost)')\n","print(f'Normalise /255     : range [0,255] -> [{f4(X.min())}, {f4(X.max())}] ; mean {f4(X.mean())}, std {f4(X.std())}')\n","print(f'Standardise (train stats only): per-pixel mean -> {f4(scaler_px.transform(X_tr).mean())}, std -> {f4(scaler_px.transform(X_tr).std())}')\n","\n","# Flattening: distance-based models cannot see spatial structure.\n","perm = rng.permutation(IMG * IMG)\n","d_orig = euclidean_distances(X_tr[:200], X_va[:50])\n","d_perm = euclidean_distances(X_tr[:200][:, perm], X_va[:50][:, perm])\n","print('Flattening: distances identical after randomly shuffling pixel order ->', np.allclose(d_orig, d_perm))\n","print('Split: max class-proportion difference train vs test =', f4(np.abs(split_tab.train - split_tab.test).max()))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"45a9158b","metadata":{"id":"45a9158b"},"source":["* **Resizing/grayscale** – removes ≈98 % of raw values; fine lesion texture and the *colour* of lesions (yellow halo vs brown spot) are lost → expected confusion between colour-defined diseases.\n","* **Normalisation /255 and standardisation** – no information lost; changes the *geometry* (feature scales) → affects conditioning (Task 4) and distance-based models.\n","* **Flattening** – the shuffled-pixel test above shows k-NN/linear models are *permutation-invariant*: spatial neighbourhood is invisible to them. A CNN uses it.\n","* **Stratified split** – keeps class proportions equal; scaler/PCA fitted on train only to avoid leakage."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"193debe6","metadata":{"id":"193debe6"},"source":["## Task 2 — Structure of the Feature Space (Eigen/SVD) (5 marks)\n","\n","**Formulas.** Centred data $X_c = X-\\mathbf{1}\\mu^\\top$ (n×d). Covariance $C=\\frac{1}{n-1}X_c^\\top X_c$.\n","Eigendecomposition $C=Q\\Lambda Q^\\top$; SVD $X_c=U\\Sigma V^\\top$. Then $C = V\\frac{\\Sigma^2}{n-1}V^\\top$, so\n","$$\\lambda_i=\\frac{\\sigma_i^2}{n-1},\\qquad \\text{EVR}_i=\\frac{\\lambda_i}{\\sum_j\\lambda_j},\\qquad \\text{rel. reconstruction error}(k)=\\frac{\\sum_{i>k}\\lambda_i}{\\sum_j\\lambda_j}.$$\n","\n","### Hand-worked 2×2 sub-problem\n","Two neighbouring pixels $(p_1,p_2)$ observed in 4 images: $(1,2),(2,1),(3,4),(4,3)$.\n","\n","1. Mean $\\mu=(2.5,\\,2.5)$. Centred rows: $(-1.5,-0.5),(-0.5,-1.5),(0.5,1.5),(1.5,0.5)$.\n","2. $\\sum p_1^2 = 2.25+0.25+0.25+2.25=5$, $\\sum p_2^2=5$, $\\sum p_1p_2=0.75\\times4=3$.\n","3. $C=\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}5&3\\\\3&5\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1.6667&1\\\\1&1.6667\\end{bmatrix}$\n","4. $\\det(C-\\lambda I)=(1.6667-\\lambda)^2-1=0 \\Rightarrow \\lambda_1=2.6667,\\ \\lambda_2=0.6667$\n","5. $\\lambda_1$: $(C-\\lambda_1I)v=0\\Rightarrow -v_1+v_2=0\\Rightarrow v_1=\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt2}(1,1)=(0.7071,0.7071)$; $\\lambda_2$: $v_2=(0.7071,-0.7071)$\n","6. EVR$_1 = 2.6667/3.3333 = 0.8000$ → one direction (\"average brightness of the pair\") holds 80 % of the variance: neighbouring pixels are **redundant**.\n","7. Singular values of $X_c$: $\\sigma_i=\\sqrt{(n-1)\\lambda_i}$ → $\\sigma_1=\\sqrt{8}=2.8284,\\ \\sigma_2=\\sqrt{2}=1.4142$."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"772b95db","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-12T04:12:26.794269Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-12T04:12:26.793779Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-12T04:12:26.813339Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-12T04:12:26.812053Z"},"id":"772b95db","outputId":"59eac15b-2b84-4fc6-f701-d7db76dbce24","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791960916163,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":76,"user":{"displayName":"Padmanabhan S","userId":"00156433950367292426"}}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["C =\n"," [[1.6667 1.    ]\n"," [1.     1.6667]]\n","eigenvalues [2.6667 0.6667] | eigenvectors\n"," [[ 0.7071 -0.7071]\n"," [ 0.7071  0.7071]]\n","singular values [2.8284 1.4142] | sigma^2/(n-1) = [2.6667 0.6667] | EVR1 = 0.8\n"]}],"source":["Xs = np.array([[1, 2], [2, 1], [3, 4], [4, 3]], float); Xs_c = Xs - Xs.mean(0)\n","C2 = Xs_c.T @ Xs_c / (len(Xs) - 1)\n","lam2, Q2 = np.linalg.eigh(C2); s2 = np.linalg.svd(Xs_c, compute_uv=False)\n","print('C =\\n', C2); print('eigenvalues', lam2[::-1].round(4), '| eigenvectors\\n', Q2[:, ::-1].round(4))\n","print('singular values', s2.round(4), '| sigma^2/(n-1) =', (s2**2 / 3).round(4), '| EVR1 =', f4(lam2[-1] / lam2.sum()))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"79b30768","metadata":{"id":"79b30768"},"source":["### SVD and Eigendecomposition of the Full Training Set\n","**Eigenvalues from singular values**\n","$$\\lambda_i=\\frac{\\sigma_i^2}{n-1}$$\n","**Explained variance ratio**\n","$$\\text{EVR}_i=\\frac{\\lambda_i}{\\sum_{j}\\lambda_j}$$\n","Both routes (SVD of $X_c$ and `eigh` of $C$) are timed and compared; $k$ for 90 / 95 / 99 % variance is reported."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"618f40a6","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-12T04:12:26.816293Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-12T04:12:26.815601Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-12T04:13:40.718622Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-12T04:13:40.717436Z"},"id":"618f40a6","outputId":"f9434f19-0c56-42dd-84e0-299e181923db","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791961014813,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":98645,"user":{"displayName":"Padmanabhan S","userId":"00156433950367292426"}}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["SVD time 86.2718 s | eigh(C) time 12.7322 s\n","max |lambda_SVD - lambda_eig| over top 50 = 0.0\n","Top-10 eigenvalues: [16.774   9.4144  8.6223  8.0118  2.2765  1.8403  1.4518  1.3877  1.3336\n","  0.8706]\n","EVR of PC1..PC5: [0.1957 0.1098 0.1006 