;\n","(iv) PC1 ≈ overall brightness/leaf-vs-background, later PCs ≈ leaf shape/orientation, *not* disease spots – variance ≠ discriminative information;\n","(v) cost grows ≈ linearly in n while n < d=4096, then the d² term dominates – eigh(C) is fixed O(d³) once n > d."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"76736af0","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-12T04:15:39.288140Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-12T04:15:39.287855Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-12T04:15:45.674927Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-12T04:15:45.674355Z"},"id":"76736af0","outputId":"7ed6a946-9f98-4491-d3fd-08dfa414e432","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791961153433,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":9064,"user":{"displayName":"Padmanabhan S","userId":"00156433950367292426"}}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["PCA features: (12712, 560) | explained variance = 0.9495000243186951\n"]}],"source":["# Shared feature sets used from here on\n","K_PCA = k95\n","pca = PCA(n_components=K_PCA, random_state=SEED).fit(X_tr)\n","Z_tr, Z_va, Z_te = pca.transform(X_tr), pca.transform(X_va), pca.transform(X_te)\n","print('PCA features:', Z_tr.shape, '| explained variance =', f4(pca.explained_variance_ratio_.sum()))\n","\n","def make_models():\n","    return {'LogReg (linear, parametric)': make_pipeline(StandardScaler(), LogisticRegression(C=1.0, max_iter=300)),\n","            'k-NN k=5 (non-parametric)': KNeighborsClassifier(5),\n","            'Random Forest (tree ensemble)': RandomForestClassifier(150, n_jobs=-1, random_state=SEED)}"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a581600b","metadata":{"id":"a581600b"},"source":["## Task 3 — Uncertainty: Probability and Information Theory (4 marks)\n","\n","**Formulas (bits):**\n","$H(p)=-\\sum_k p_k\\log_2 p_k$, $\\quad H(p,q)=-\\sum_k p_k\\log_2 q_k$, $\\quad D_{KL}(p\\|q)=\\sum_k p_k\\log_2\\frac{p_k}{q_k}$, $\\quad H(p,q)=H(p)+D_{KL}(p\\|q)$.\n","\n","Per-image the true distribution is one-hot, so $H(\\mathbf e_y)=0$ and $H(\\mathbf e_y,q)=D_{KL}(\\mathbf e_y\\|q)=-\\log_2 q_y$ (the log-loss)."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"446c3aba","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-12T04:15:45.679288Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-12T04:15:45.679051Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-12T04:15:45.702801Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-12T04:15:45.701631Z"},"id":"446c3aba","outputId":"90ff6603-5210-4e14-81e8-fc1d65e7bebf","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791961153566,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":130,"user":{"displayName":"Padmanabhan S","userId":"00156433950367292426"}}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["class prior p = [0.1171 0.0551 0.1052 0.0524 0.0975 0.0924 0.0773 0.295  0.0205 0.0876]\n","H(p) = 3.03 bits | max log2(K) = 3.3219 | normalised H = 0.9121\n","Majority-class accuracy = 0.295 | chance (uniform) = 0.1\n"]}],"source":["def H(p): p = np.asarray(p, float); p = p[p > 0]; return -(p * np.log2(p)).sum()\n","def CE(p, q, eps=1e-12): return -(np.asarray(p) * np.log2(np.clip(q, eps, 1))).sum()\n","def KL(p, q, eps=1e-12):\n","    p, q = np.asarray(p, float), np.clip(np.asarray(q, float), eps, 1); m = p > 0\n","    return (p[m] * np.log2(p[m] / q[m])).sum()\n","\n","p_cls = np.bincount(y_tr, minlength=K) / len(y_tr)\n","print('class prior p =', p_cls.round(4))\n","print(f'H(p) = {f4(H(p_cls))} bits | max log2(K) = {f4(np.log2(K))} | normalised H = {f4(H(p_cls) / np.log2(K))}')\n","print('Majority-class accuracy =', f4(p_cls.max()), '| chance (uniform) =', f4(1 / K))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"94486068","metadata":{"id":"94486068"},"source":["### Cross-Entropy and KL Divergence of the Three Models\n","**Per-image log-loss** (one-hot truth, so $H(\\mathbf e_y)=0$)\n","$$H(\\mathbf e_y,q)=D_{KL}(\\mathbf e_y\\|q)=-\\log_2 q_y$$\n","**Distribution level** ($p$ = validation class frequencies, $\\bar q$ = mean predicted distribution)\n","$$H(p,\\bar q)=H(p)+D_{KL}(p\\|\\bar q)$$"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"982b9b2b","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-12T04:15:45.706249Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-12T04:15:45.705978Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-12T04:16:15.749798Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-12T04:16:15.748047Z"},"id":"982b9b2b","outputId":"71ebff05-1009-4b5f-fd6d-0c0e763e820b","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":247},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791961214874,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":61304,"user":{"displayName":"Padmanabhan S","userId":"00156433950367292426"}}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["                           model  val acc  per-image CE = KL (bits)  \\\n","0    LogReg (linear, parametric)   0.4677                    2.6171   \n","1      k-NN k=5 (non-parametric)   0.4640                   11.7051   \n","2  Random Forest (tree ensemble)   0.4805                    2.3540   \n","\n","   frac q_y = 0  H(p_val)  H(p, q̄)  KL(p||q̄)  KL(q̄||p)  mean pred. entropy  \n","0        0.0000    3.0298    3.0314     0.0016     0.0017              1.7856  \n","1        0.2757    3.0298    3.1897     0.1599     0.1438              0.9420  \n","2        0.0004    3.0298    3.0312     0.0014     0.0014              2.7957  "],"text/html":["\n","  <div id=\"df-29349e82-67ba-4a78-82d1-3f0f7c8ff08d\" class=\"colab-df-container\">\n","    <div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>model</th>\n","      <th>val acc</th>\n","      <th>per-image CE = KL (bits)</th>\n","      <th>frac q_y = 0</th>\n","      <th