(steps)), steps, lw=.6, alpha=.7, label=nm)\n","    rows.append([nm, bs, f4(lr), ups, f4(tt / EP), f4(hist[-1]), f4(np.std(steps[-ups:])), f4(accuracy_score(y_va, (Fv_w @ W).argmax(1)))])\n","ax[0].set(title='Full-train loss per epoch (whitened PCA-50)', xlabel='epoch', ylabel='J(W)'); ax[0].legend(fontsize=8)\n","ax[1].set(title='Per-update mini-batch loss (noise of the path)', xlabel='epoch', ylabel='batch loss', ylim=(0, None)); ax[1].legend(fontsize=8)\n","plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n","display(pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=['strategy', 'batch', 'η', 'updates/epoch', 'sec/epoch', 'final loss', 'loss noise (sd, last epoch)', 'val acc']))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"905150da","metadata":{"id":"905150da"},"source":["### Effect of the Learning Rate\n","Batch GD with $\\eta\\in\\{0.05,\\ 0.5,\\ 0.95,\\ 3.0\\}\\times\\eta_{crit}$ on ill-conditioned and well-conditioned inputs.\n","**Stability condition**\n","$$0<\\eta<\\frac{2}{\\lambda_{\\max}}$$"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"1488ec04","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-12T04:23:02.370958Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-12T04:23:02.370669Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-12T04:23:22.474831Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-12T04:23:22.474086Z"},"id":"1488ec04"},"outputs":[],"source":["EPG = 30 if TEST_MODE else 150\n","mults = [0.05, 0.5, 0.95, 3.0]\n","fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 4)); rows = []\n","for a, (nm, F, crit) in zip(ax, [('unwhitened (ill-conditioned)', F_raw, eta_crit_raw), ('whitened (well-conditioned)', F_w, eta_crit_w)]):\n","    for mlt in mults:\n","        lr = mlt * crit; _, hist, _, _ = train_softmax(F, Ytr, lr, len(F), EPG)\n","        a.plot(hist, label=f'η = {mlt}·η_crit = {lr:.3g}')\n","        fin = hist[np.isfinite(hist)]\n","        rows.append([nm, mlt, f4(lr), f4(fin[-1]) if len(fin) else np.nan, int(np.argmax(hist < 1.01 * np.nanmin(hist))) if len(fin) else np.nan,\n","                     'diverged/oscillating' if (len(fin) < EPG or np.any(np.diff(fin[:10]) > 0)) else 'stable'])\n","    a.set(title=f'Batch GD – {nm}', xlabel='epoch', ylabel='J(W)', yscale='log'); a.legend(fontsize=8)\n","plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n","lr_tab = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=['features', 'η / η_crit', 'η', 'final loss', 'epochs to within 1% of best', 'behaviour']); display(lr_tab)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"94228812","metadata":{"id":"94228812"},"source":["**Points to analyse:** batch GD – smooth path, one update per epoch (expensive per step, cheap per epoch in vectorised NumPy);\n","SGD – N noisy updates per epoch, jagged path, reaches low loss in few epochs but plateaus at a noise floor; mini-batch – compromise, vectorised.\n","Learning rate: small η → slow; η near η_crit → fastest; η > η_crit → overshoots/oscillates or diverges. Unwhitened features have large κ (Task 4):\n","the stable η is forced small by $\\lambda_{\\max}$ so low-variance PC directions learn very slowly → whitening (κ=1) converges far faster."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"4173cbe3","metadata":{"id":"4173cbe3"},"source":["## Task 9 — Experimental Performance across Dataset Scales (3 marks)\n","\n","Scales use stratified subsets of the train+val pool; every model is evaluated on the **same locked test set**.\n","Metrics: $\\text{Precision}=\\frac{TP}{TP+FP}$, $\\text{Recall}=\\frac{TP}{TP+FN}$, $F_1=\\frac{2PR}{P+R}$ (macro-averaged over classes)."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"613d483d","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-12T04:23:22.478446Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-12T04:23:22.478213Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-12T04:29:30.127056Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-12T04:29:30.125478Z"},"id":"613d483d","outputId":"633d557e-08f5-4398-afc5-ea19c4371142","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":978},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791962366556,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":328835,"user":{"displayName":"Padmanabhan S","userId":"00156433950367292426"}}},"outputs":[